capability address/integer  an IPv4 address as the integer of its 32 bits, and back
  heroes  net.from_integer, net.to_integer
  go      -
  rust    Ipv4Addr::from_bits, Ipv4Addr::to_bits, Ipv6Addr::from_bits, Ipv6Addr::to_bits, Ipv4Addr::steps_between
  python  int(IPv4Address), ipaddress.IPv4Address(int), int(IPv6Address), ipaddress.IPv6Address(int)
  note    IPv6's 128 bits are past every Heroes integer, so `to_integer` fails `invalid` on one; the steps between two IPv4 addresses are the difference of their integers

